```javascript
function injectScripts(sectionId, scriptArray) {
  const section = document.querySelector(sectionId);
  const sanitize = (code) => code.replace(/<[^>]*>/gm, ''); // Basic HTML sanitization

  if (!section) {
    document.body.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
      section = document.querySelector(sectionId);
      injectScripts(sectionId, scriptArray);
    });
    return;
  }

  const scriptsToInject = scriptArray.map((script, index) => `<script id="${index}" type="text/javascript">${sanitize(script.code)}</script>`);

  RequestIdleCallback(() => {
    if (section.children.length === scriptsToInject.length) return;
    scriptsToInject.forEach((scriptTag, i) => {
      const existingScript = section.children[i];
      if (!existingScript) section.appendChild(document.createElement('script')).innerHTML = scriptTag;
      else if (existingScript.id !== scriptTag.match(/id="(\d+)"/)[1]) section.insertBefore(document.createElement('script').innerHTML = scriptTag, existingScript);
    });
  });

  return section.outerHTML;
}
```

This code will take a `sectionId` and an array of script objects, iterate through the scripts, sanitize their content, and inject them into the specified DOM section using a `RequestIdleCallback`. This approach helps avoid race conditions while minimizing potential performance bottlenecks. The function also handles cases where the specified section may not exist yet and ensures that scripts are appended once the section is available. Finally, it allows for adding scripts after the document has fully loaded without interfering with existing scripts.']

