The implementation is backward-compatible with third-party libraries, as it leverages the built-in `BinaryFormatter` class for serialization. Error handling is implemented for corrupted or incomplete files, and temporary interruptions are gracefully handled without losing data. The solution is scalable to accommodate future growth in file size and complexity.

To integrate with an existing data processing pipeline, simply process the deserialized objects as needed within the `foreach` loop at the end of the `ProcessFileAsync` method.']

