To optimize for performance, consider using more efficient data structures or lock-free constructs when possible, and reducing the frequency of resizing operations by estimating how many elements will be needed in advance. Additionally, you may want to explore techniques such as thread pooling, work queues, or other concurrency patterns to manage the 100 threads efficiently.']

