For integers, the default implementation uses a simple algorithm based on the System.Random class. For floating-point numbers, it uses the same underlying `System.Random` class but ensures proper range limits are applied. You can replace the default generator with custom implementations that may use more advanced algorithms or provide additional features.

The generated values are wrapped as objects to support different data types while maintaining type safety. The logging and monitoring capabilities can be added by integrating this class with existing logging frameworks, such as Microsoft's System.Diagnostics.Trace or Serilog.

