It utilizes a linked list to manage RNTIs, which helps prevent memory fragmentation and optimize for multi-threaded environments. The memory usage is monitored using `mmap` and `msync`, adjusting the memory threshold as needed. Performance metrics are logged for debugging and monitoring purposes.

The function has been optimized for performance by minimizing memory usage, utilizing a pseudo-random number generator with user-provided seed, and leveraging appropriate synchronization mechanisms (`pthread_mutex_lock`/`pthread_mutex_unlock`) to ensure thread safety and avoid data races.

Edge cases such as when `N` is very large or when system memory is limited have been considered in the code. The external logging library is used for detailed logs during debugging and monitoring.']

