The function `crci_list_add()` adds a PDU to the list, ensuring that the RNTI value is unique within the list. The function `crci_list_get()` retrieves a PDU based on the given RNTI, and optionally uses cached RNTIs to optimize performance.

The function `crci_list_free()` frees any allocated resources when no longer needed. Error handling is implemented for memory allocation failures, RNTI conflicts, and other runtime errors using careful use of `malloc`, `calloc`, and explicit checks on input parameters.']

